{
 "schema": "terluna.research.open-moon-aerosol/1",
 "evidence": "A structured estimate. Each region's particles near the ground are a measured Earth analogue (the clean wet-season Amazon, the remote ocean by day, the Arctic summer) changed by lunar factors from the literature notes on the data drive (aerosol_marine.md, aerosol_biogenic.md, aerosol_dust_fog.md, aerosol_budget.md) and the project's own models: the regions' areas from the GCM and geography, their weather near the ground from CM1's rings, the ionization from the conductivity column. Clean, central and loaded cases run from the fewest particles to the most. Nothing here is a measurement of the Open Moon; the design levers and the gaps are listed with the results.",
 "reading_rule": "Number concentrations per cm3; diameters in nm (dry medians of lognormal modes); conductivity in S/m at the ground (2 m), total of both signs; relaxation time eps0/sigma in minutes. Day and night are hour angles within and beyond 95 degrees of noon. The night values are means over the dark hours; \"with fog\" weights the clear and foggy conductivity by the share of hours in fog. Area shares are of the whole Moon. CCN at 0.1, 0.3 and 1 % supersaturation.",
